LockIntegrationConcreteTest
├── When the lockUntil is lower or equal to timestamp
│   └── It should revert with {InvalidLockTime}
└── When the lockUntil is greater than timestamp
    ├── When the beneficiary is not address zero
    │   ├── When the beneficiary share is zero or greater than MAX_BPS
    │   │   └── It should revert with {InvalidBeneficiaryShare}
    │   └── When the beneficiary share is not zero nor greater than MAX_BPS
    │       ├── When the bribeable share is greater than MAX_BPS
    │       │   └── It should revert with {InvalidBribeableShare}
    │       └── When the bribeable share is smaller or equal to MAX_BPS
    │           ├── When the position to lock does not exist in the Nfpm
    │           │   └── It should revert with {ID}
    │           └── When the position to lock exists in the Nfpm
    │               ├── When the caller is not the pool launcher
    │               │   ├── It should update locked liquidity
    │               │   ├── It should increment the number of locks
    │               │   ├── It should create the new lock
    │               │   ├── It should pull the LP from the user to the locker
    │               │   ├── It should set the instances mapping
    │               │   └── It should emit a {LockerCreated} event
    │               └── When the caller is the pool launcher
    │                   ├── It should update locked liquidity
    │                   ├── It should increment the number of locks
    │                   ├── It should create the new lock
    │                   ├── It shoult transfer the LP to the locker
    │                   ├── It should set the instances mapping
    │                   └── It should emit a {LockerCreated} event
    └── When the beneficiary is address zero
        ├── When the bribeable share is greater than MAX_BPS_
        │   └── It should revert with {InvalidBribeableShare}
        └── When the bribeable share is smaller or equal to MAX_BPS_
            ├── When the position to lock does not exist in the Nfpm_
            │   └── It should revert with {ID}
            └── When the position to lock exists in the Nfpm_
                ├── When the caller is not the pool launcher_
                │   ├── It should update locked liquidity
                │   ├── It should increment the number of locks
                │   ├── It should create the new lock
                │   ├── It should pull the LP from the user to the locker
                │   ├── It should set the instances mapping
                │   └── It should emit a {LockerCreated} event
                └── When the caller is the pool launcher_
                    ├── It should update locked liquidity
                    ├── It should increment the number of locks
                    ├── It should create the new lock
                    ├── It shoult transfer the LP to the locker
                    ├── It should set the instances mapping
                    └── It should emit a {LockerCreated} event
